WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.740
- All right, y'all, we've got
time for one last quick story

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.340
that will put a smile
on your face hopefully.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.525
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:08.740
(cheery music)
(audience claps)

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.250
So, mamas, all of us
at one point have felt

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.660
like the worst parent on earth,

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.550
and if you haven't, that's
probably cuz you are (laughs).

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.383
(audience laughs)

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.590
Whether it's forgetting to
pack a diaper bag (laughs),

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.200
serving your kid chicken
nuggets five days in a row,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.260
you've done it, or letting
your kid play Roblox

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.220
for, I don't know, four hours straight,

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.520
cuz you just needed a minute.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.680
We've all been there.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.513
I haven't.

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:31.346
I'm perfect,

00:00:31.346 --> 00:00:32.870
but you've been there maybe.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.180
So in solidarity, let's
spare some sympathy

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.430
for a Minnesota mama who
realized, this is amazing,

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.150
after years, years,

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.460
that she was celebrating
her son's birthday (laughs)

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.570
on the wrong date.
(audience groans)

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.610
Take a look.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.550
- I just got off the phone
with my pediatrician.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.880
She's trying to bill our last visit

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.280
to our insurance company.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.467
Per my words, "My son's
birthday is the 26th.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:57.967
"I'm his mother.

00:00:57.967 --> 00:00:59.070
"I know his birthday."

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.287
The insurance company says,

00:01:00.287 --> 00:01:02.901
"No, his birthday's on the 25th."

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:06.210
For two years, I've been
celebrating his birthday

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.270
on the 26th.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.570
You wanna know the worst part?

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.170
The worst part.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.703
It's my middle child.

00:01:11.703 --> 00:01:14.912
(Kelly laughs)
(audience groans and claps)

00:01:14.912 --> 00:01:16.050
- Oh, my God.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.490
The best part of that
is my sister is going

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:20.323
to love that part.

00:01:20.323 --> 00:01:21.690
She's the middle child, the bereft child,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.260
everything didn't happen for her.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.180
We have that mom, Emily,
on the line right now.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.013
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:28.333
Emily, I love you.

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:30.359
(audience cheers)

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:31.203
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:31.203 --> 00:01:32.036
- This is so funny.

00:01:32.036 --> 00:01:32.960
I've just never heard of it.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.320
So wait, your insurance company is

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.510
actually how you found out

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:36.710
that you were celebrating
your son's birthday

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.620
on the wrong day.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.290
- Yes, so my pediatrician's
office calls me

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.200
cuz she can't bill the visit.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.933
The birthdate I gave her is wrong is

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:45.660
what the insurance company is saying,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.130
and I was about to call
the insurance company

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.320
and give them a piece of my
mind cuz I know his birthday.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.510
I'm his mother.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.740
But before I called them, I thought

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.220
maybe I should scroll back
Facebook just to make sure.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.800
And sure enough, the insurance
company had it right.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.050
Of course, they did (Emily laughs).

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.540
And it made stickin' national news,

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.120
my mom fail, heard 'round the world.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.730
Gosh.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.860
- Wait, that's the best part too.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.760
You didn't like fail alone though.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.862
Your husband didn't know either.

00:02:14.862 --> 00:02:15.695
(Emily groans in disgust)

00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:17.640
- If this was my husband's mistake,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.722
it wouldn't be national news.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:21.280
I asked him the other night,

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.490
do you know any of our kids' birthdays?

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:27.720
And, we have four kids, and
he got the birth months right,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.450
but zero of the dates.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.790
So.
(Kelly cackles)

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.090
- You're like, so you know what?

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.900
Crawl under this bus
with me, sir (laughs).

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.790
I was like, oh my God, I love it.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.130
This is one of my favorite
mom fails I've ever heard of.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.260
I love you so much.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.160
Congratulations.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.250
It's his birthday today as well.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.083
I'm claiming it.

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.790
This is Henry's birthday as well.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.522
I'm liking your post right now, okay?

00:02:48.522 --> 00:02:50.010
(bell dings)

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.020
It's just never not
gonna be funny (laughs).

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:52.853
Oh, my God.

00:02:52.853 --> 00:02:53.740
Okay, so that's not all.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.420
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.020
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.150
wanna honor mamas just like you

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.160
cuz you're working hard at it.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.640
You got a lot of kids, girl.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.450
Congratulations, they're
gonna write you a check

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.463
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:05.463 --> 00:03:07.477
(audience cheers)

00:03:07.477 --> 00:03:09.206
- Oh, my gosh.

00:03:09.206 --> 00:03:10.616
I did not know this.

00:03:10.616 --> 00:03:11.877
- See, your mom fail paid off.

